WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.400
Hand off from Claude Code to Codex at a usage limit.

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:10.522
With specweave auto-handoff on, Claude Code sends its usage to SpecWeave.

3
00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:15.507
Here we pass in a sample reading of 95% of the 5-hour limit.

4
00:00:15.507 --> 00:00:19.230
The guard says a handoff is available, and work continues.

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.470
When you are ready, tell Claude to hand off.

6
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.910
It runs specweave handoff with a reason,

7
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:29.380
releases its claim on T-02, and writes handoff.md.

8
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:34.559
handoff.md says who stopped and why, and which tasks are done.

9
00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:38.605
It lists the uncommitted files, with the full diff beside it,

10
00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.530
and the exact next step.

11
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.683
Now open Codex in the same repo and say "pick up".

12
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:47.940
It runs specweave pickup, which reads the handoff

13
00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.640
and records the pickup in the ledger as codex@demo.

14
00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.882
Pickup names the next task, T-02,

15
00:00:54.882 --> 00:00:58.802
with its acceptance criterion, its files and its test.

16
00:00:58.802 --> 00:01:00.190
Codex claims it.

17
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.968
With the change in place,

18
00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:05.977
task done --run runs the test again.

19
00:01:05.977 --> 00:01:09.120
Only a passing test marks the task done,

20
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.910
and the ledger shows that Codex finished it.

21
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:17.080
Next, specweave verify checks the increment before you close it.
